      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin (2,550 mg/day), and the extended-release maximum is lower still (2,000\u20132,500 mg/day depending on the product). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI intolerance, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), the usual IR maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day), a common target dose.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, if the intended figure was a daily total. For example, 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or whether 1700 mg was a typo, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
