       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The claim that 5,100 mg/day is within the current FDA label doesn't match what I know. The labeled maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg, and it is 2,000 mg for most extended-release products. I can't check the label from here, and your confirmation doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **Metformin 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Metformin 1,700 mg PO once daily**, or a split such as 850 mg twice daily, if 1,700 mg was meant as the daily total\n\nIf you think there's a clinical reason to go above the label, such as a different formulation or a protocol, please take it to pharmacy or the prescriber of record. They can review it and place the order through the appropriate channel. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
